they can now say goodbye to Carmen and put her soul to rest as she deserves. The family will now have the opportunity to start rebuilding their lives. Police believed Carmen may have been killed because she saw Mr. Krull's face, causing him to panic and shoot her three times in the head. They believed this based on something that had been previously attributed to Mr. Krull. In February 1985, a 14-year-old girl was abducted by a masked man from her home in Hampton, at Bayside suburb in southeast Melbourne. The man bound, gagged and blindfolded the girl before driving her to a vacant building site,

