00:53:24.000 --> 00:54:21.000
killing her. It also appeared that he had lain low ever since, with no further offences relating to the Mr. Cruel M.O. reported after Carmen Chan's abduction. In the absence of any viable leads, investigators turned to increasingly unorthodox methods in the hopes they might lead to the killer. detectives believed that Mr. Cruel may have suffered from anxiety, stress and depression after Carmen's murder and perhaps sought treatment for these ailments. They wrote to every single one of Victoria's 10,000 registered doctors asking them to consider breaking patient confidentiality and think about whether their duty to the community outweighed duty to a patient. The doctors were also sent a profile of Mr. Cruel the dates of the crimes and other information about the case.

